<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-17 — wizard→review auto-run bridge (fileId impedance + durable bind + silent-FK fix)</title>
    <phase>3 Durable Review</phase>
    <gate>blocked (deps 023,031)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Cross-surface bridge (wizard→session→dispatch) incl. a BFF fix (ChatSessionManager); the owner's Phase-2 must-have leg; auth+durability semantics.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The impedance bridge (durable sprk_document → session file context) has no precedent to copy — it is the one genuinely novel integration in the project, with server+client legs and failure-mode design.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>H</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>023,031</deps>
    <tags>spaarkeai, bff, ai, durable-recall</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    On Create-Analysis wizard finish (agreement work-type): bridge the durable sprk_document into session file context,
    bind the session durably to the Analysis, auto-dispatch the agreement review, and render advisory comments in the
    already-open editable Compose — no manual re-upload. Fix (or design around, with proof) the promote silent-FK gap:
    a 201 that writes no durable Dataverse FK is unacceptable for legal work product.
  </prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Session dispatch file resolution, fork/promote contracts, wizard finish seam, BFF durability.</role>
  <goal>Wizard-finish yields: bound session (visible via by-analysis), review dispatched on the right pack, comments in Compose — one flow, durable.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Verified impedance (HUB-R1-REVIEW §5): the wizard produces a durable sprk_document
      (sprk_graphitemid/sprk_graphdriveid via EntityCreationService, CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx master :636-658);
      dispatch consumes SESSION-uploaded fileIds only (SessionDispatchOrchestrator.ResolveTargetFiles :689-769, hard
      error "No session files were available" :769). NO bridge exists; the wizard creates NO session and runs NO review
      (hub HANDOFF-2026-07-31 §4 verbatim). BRIDGE DESIGN: register the durable doc as the session's file context
      before dispatch — investigate the session file-registration seam (compose.upload/stored → speDriveItemId
      addressing; the compose seed already carries SPE pointers) — prefer registering the SPE pointer as a session file
      over re-uploading bytes. BIND: wizard-finish has no session yet → create session with HostContext sentinel
      (EntityType="sprk_analysisoutput", EntityId=analysisId — the FOOTGUN: EntityId is an sprk_analysis GUID; never
      query the output table with it) — via fork (mints bound session; requires documentId+name) or create-then-promote;
      promote requires documentId and is one-time-bind. SILENT-FK FIX: PromoteSessionToAnalysisAsync ignores
      BindSessionToAnalysisAsync's bool (ChatSessionManager.cs:527; repo tolerates missing summary row :261-272) —
      propagate the failure (retry-create the summary row, else non-2xx/warning surfaced). Hub Q2 default: we fix it.
      PHASE-1 UAT: the wizard-finish seam may change under owner UAT — check status first (escalation).
      SUBDOMAIN: the wizard envelope carries subDomain (A1/A3) — 023's explicit bind picks the pack; auto-dispatch uses it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx (finish hook)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs (silent-FK fix)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/AnalysisEndpoints.cs (fork :1136 / promote :1285 contracts)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SessionDispatchOrchestrator.cs (ResolveTargetFiles)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">explicit-path pack bind (which review to run)</dependency>
      <dependency task="031" status="pending">document-session routing (where the output lands)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">File access via the SpeFileStore facade / existing SPE-pointer addressing — do NOT re-upload bytes the wizard already stored; scope: the bridge.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Client→AI via existing endpoints/facade; any new BFF surface needs §10 Placement Justification + publish-size check; scope: server changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">documentId/analysisId GUIDs canonical bare-lowercase across the fork/promote/OData calls; scope: all IDs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Sentinel footgun: HostContext.EntityId under EntityType "sprk_analysisoutput" is an sprk_analysis GUID — reference an existing sentinel constant site, never re-type the literal; never query the output table with it. Scope: bind wiring.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Durable-bind acceptance: after finish, GET /sessions/by-analysis/{analysisId} returns the session — the silent-FK gap must be closed on THIS path (fix promote, or use fork whose create-time FK write must equally be verified). Scope: bind + fix.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">New failure paths (bridge failure, bind failure) return/surface ProblemDetails-consistent errors — the wizard shows a real error, not silent success. Scope: error handling.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Session file resolution + fork/promote + wizard seam</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-044-dataverse-guid-canonicalization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1/notes/HUB-R1-REVIEW-2026-07-30.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fork/promote contracts" location="projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-agreements-r1/notes/HUB-R1-REVIEW-2026-07-30.md §3">Exact request/response shapes + caveats — call as documented; verify against code at task time.</pattern>
      <pattern name="compose seed SPE addressing" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx (:618-658)">Where the durable doc's SPE pointers are in hand at finish time.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor; check Phase-1 owner-UAT status (hub Q5) — if the finish seam is changing, escalate before building; audit the session file-registration seam (does an SPE-pointer registration path exist?).</step>
    <step order="1">Design the bridge (pointer-registration preferred; document the §11 extension answers) + the bind choice (fork vs create-then-promote) for the no-session-yet finish case.</step>
    <step order="2">Fix the silent-FK gap in ChatSessionManager/ChatDataverseRepository (propagate bind result; retry-create summary row; surface failure) + unit test.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the finish hook: bridge file → bind session → auto-dispatch (per 023's pack) → comments render via 030/031's durable path.</step>
    <step order="4">Failure modes: bridge/bind/dispatch failures surface distinctly in the wizard + Assistant; no silent partial success.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: unit (FK fix), integration (bind visible via by-analysis), e2e happy path; BFF publish-size check (server touched).</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: 033 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If no session file-registration seam exists and the bridge requires a NEW BFF endpoint or dispatch-contract change, STOP — present the §10/§11-justified minimal server delta before building.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Phase-1 owner UAT is still open on the wizard-finish seam, STOP and confirm the seam is stable (hub Q5) before wiring into it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">BFF build/tests + publish-size</tool><tool name="npm">widgets build/tests</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">CreateAnalysisWizardWidget.tsx finish hook + ChatSessionManager.cs FK fix + bridge wiring</output>
    <output type="test">FK-fix unit test + bind-visibility integration test</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Wizard-finish on an agreement: review auto-runs on the selected type's pack; advisory comments render in the open Compose; no manual re-upload.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /sessions/by-analysis/{analysisId} returns the bound session (durable FK proven) — the silent-FK gap cannot produce a 201-without-FK on this path (regression test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dispatch resolves the bridged file (no "No session files were available" error).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: bridge failure / bind failure / dispatch failure each surface a distinct visible error; the Analysis record's state remains consistent (no orphan half-flows).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish ≤60 MB reported; no new HIGH CVE; build + tests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-17; hub Phase-2 leg + Part C.4; hub Q2 default (we fix the FK). With 030-032, completes the owner's 3-phase must-have.</notes>
  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
